WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.281
Welcome to The Fantastical Logic Grid.

2
00:00:03.431 --> 00:00:07.677
Every puzzle is a brand new story, and you are
the detective.

3
00:00:08.477 --> 00:00:12.061
Each puzzle is a logic grid wrapped in a
story.

4
00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:15.761
The story sets up a mystery, the clues give
you the facts,

5
00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:18.761
and the grid is where you work out the answer.

6
00:00:19.561 --> 00:00:23.423
Every story is written fresh for you and never
repeated.

7
00:00:23.573 --> 00:00:28.395
And every puzzle has exactly one answer you
can reach without guessing.

8
00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.860
Here's how to play.

9
00:00:31.695 --> 00:00:35.323
Start on the New puzzle screen and pick a
difficulty.

10
00:00:35.473 --> 00:00:38.609
Basic and Easy are perfect for beginners.

11
00:00:38.759 --> 00:00:41.149
MENSA is for true masterminds.

12
00:00:41.949 --> 00:00:46.878
Next, choose a theme, like Mystery, Fantasy,
Sci-Fi, Sports or Pets.

13
00:00:47.028 --> 00:00:48.821
Or pick Surprise me.

14
00:00:49.621 --> 00:00:51.221
Then pick a size.

15
00:00:51.371 --> 00:00:55.447
More categories and more items make a bigger,
harder grid.

16
00:00:56.247 --> 00:00:59.895
Full experience adds scenes, characters and
sound.

17
00:01:00.045 --> 00:01:05.166
Silent mode keeps only the story, the grid,
the clues and the answer key.

18
00:01:05.966 --> 00:01:10.148
Press Generate puzzle, and your story is
written in a moment.

19
00:01:10.948 --> 00:01:12.762
Read the story first.

20
00:01:12.912 --> 00:01:18.097
It tells you who is involved, and it ends with
the question you need to answer.

21
00:01:18.247 --> 00:01:20.957
Here, it's: who was holding the Silk Glove?

22
00:01:21.107 --> 00:01:24.478
You can also press Read the story aloud to
hear it.

23
00:01:25.278 --> 00:01:29.161
Select a character's portrait to hear the
clues they remember.

24
00:01:29.311 --> 00:01:32.043
Every clue is also in the clue list.

25
00:01:32.843 --> 00:01:38.625
On your first Easy puzzle, coach tips appear
above the grid to guide your first moves.

26
00:01:39.425 --> 00:01:40.791
Now the grid.

27
00:01:40.941 --> 00:01:45.208
Each square is where two things meet, like a
suspect and an age.

28
00:01:45.358 --> 00:01:48.708
Your job is to decide whether they go
together.

29
00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:52.367
Click or tap a square once to mark an X.

30
00:01:52.517 --> 00:01:56.059
X means ruled out: these two don't go
together.

31
00:01:56.859 --> 00:02:01.233
Tap again for an O. O means confirmed: these
two are a match.

32
00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:03.752
Tap a third time to clear the square.

33
00:02:04.552 --> 00:02:08.371
Let's solve one together, starting with the
simplest clue.

34
00:02:08.521 --> 00:02:14.303
Clue 7 says Greta is 35, so mark an O where
Greta meets 35.

35
00:02:15.103 --> 00:02:20.565
Each suspect has exactly one age, and each age
belongs to one suspect.

36
00:02:20.715 --> 00:02:26.241
So the rest of Greta's row and the rest of the
35 column are all X.

37
00:02:27.041 --> 00:02:31.906
Tip: turn on Auto-X in Settings and the game
fills those in for you.

38
00:02:32.706 --> 00:02:36.931
Clue 3 says whoever held the Brass Key is not
35.

39
00:02:37.081 --> 00:02:40.175
That's an X where 35 meets Brass Key.

40
00:02:40.975 --> 00:02:47.226
Clue 1 says neither the 50-year-old nor the
45-year-old held the Fountain Pen.

41
00:02:47.376 --> 00:02:49.105
Two more X marks.

42
00:02:49.905 --> 00:02:51.633
Now combine clues.

43
00:02:51.783 --> 00:02:55.837
Clue 6 says the Fountain Pen holder is 50 or
40.

44
00:02:55.987 --> 00:03:00.191
Clue 1 already ruled out 50, so it must be 40.

45
00:03:00.341 --> 00:03:04.480
Mark the O, then rule out the rest of that row
and column.

46
00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:10.657
Clue 2 says neither the Brass Key holder nor
the Silk Glove holder is 50.

47
00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:16.599
Look along the 50 row. Only the Letter Opener
is left, so that's an O.

48
00:03:16.749 --> 00:03:21.784
When only one square is left in a row or
column, it must be the answer.

49
00:03:22.584 --> 00:03:25.577
The same idea finishes this section:

50
00:03:25.597 --> 00:03:30.350
the Brass Key goes with 45, and the Silk Glove
with 35.

51
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.485
A finished section glows.

52
00:03:33.285 --> 00:03:38.512
In the full experience, each finished section
also reveals more of the scene.

53
00:03:39.312 --> 00:03:41.254
Now connect the sections.

54
00:03:41.404 --> 00:03:46.311
Greta is 35, and the 35-year-old held the Silk
Glove.

55
00:03:46.461 --> 00:03:51.006
So Greta held the Silk Glove. That answers the
story's question!

56
00:03:51.806 --> 00:03:53.343
Stuck? Press Hint.

57
00:03:53.493 --> 00:03:55.733
The first hint points you to a clue.

58
00:03:56.533 --> 00:04:00.651
Press Show more for the exact square, and then
the full reasoning.

59
00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:03.725
You can even let it mark the square for you.

60
00:04:04.525 --> 00:04:08.600
Press Check at any time to see whether any of
your marks are wrong.

61
00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:14.969
Made a mistake? Undo and Redo take back any
move, as many times as you like.

62
00:04:15.769 --> 00:04:20.825
Prefer words to grids? List view lets you
choose each match from a menu.

63
00:04:20.975 --> 00:04:25.200
The game also works fully by keyboard and with
a screen reader.

64
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.078
When you think you know, answer the questions
under the clues, and press Check answers.

65
00:04:31.878 --> 00:04:34.460
Fill in the whole grid to close the case.

66
00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:36.519
Case closed!

67
00:04:36.669 --> 00:04:41.854
You get the story's ending, your time, and a
suggestion for your next puzzle.

68
00:04:42.654 --> 00:04:45.087
Your progress saves automatically.

69
00:04:45.237 --> 00:04:49.824
Come back any time and pick up where you left
off, from Saved puzzles.

70
00:04:50.624 --> 00:04:54.344
You can also print any puzzle, blank or with
your marks,

71
00:04:54.364 --> 00:04:56.918
with the answer key on its own page.

72
00:04:57.718 --> 00:05:00.599
Press Help to see every keyboard shortcut.

73
00:05:01.399 --> 00:05:03.639
Play in light or dark colors,

74
00:05:04.439 --> 00:05:06.275
or in high contrast.

75
00:05:07.075 --> 00:05:11.235
And Silent mode is always there when you just
want the puzzle.

76
00:05:12.035 --> 00:05:17.775
That's all you need: read the story, follow
the clues, and mark your X's and O's.

77
00:05:17.925 --> 00:05:22.128
Welcome to The Fantastical Logic Grid. Happy
sleuthing!

